TOBIAS
(turning to her)
Because if I stop waiting, I have to admit what the sea took. I have to say his name out loud, here, where he learned to swim, where he laughed at the cold, where he promised me he would always come back before the lamp was lit. And he always did, Mara. Every single night until the one night he did not.

Mara takes his hand.

